course: dictionary
lesson: 1619
title: Names in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A capital letter often tells you a word is a name, such as a people, a place or a language. «Native peoples of North America were many nations with hundreds of languages, such as the Cherokee, Navajo, Lakota and Inuit.» The list of nations shows that Cherokee is the name of a people.
explain: The same word can mean different things. «The Cherokee language has its own writing system.» Here Cherokee names a language, not a people. Always ask what the sentence is about, then check whether the word fits that meaning.
explain: Context clues can also show you what happened. «On the Trail of Tears in the 1830s the Cherokee were forced to walk far west, and thousands died.» These words tell you the Cherokee were a people who lost their homelands, so the story is about history, not a car or a town.
fact: The Cherokee are a Native American people, originally from the south-east of what is now the USA.
fact: Many Cherokee people now live in Oklahoma and North Carolina.
fact: Sequoyah created a writing system for the Cherokee language.
fact: The Trail of Tears was a forced march west in the 1830s, and many Cherokee people died on the journey.
fact: Cherokee is also the name of a car model and of some places, so check the context to see which meaning is right.
exercise: «Native peoples of North America were many nations with hundreds of languages, such as the Cherokee, Navajo, Lakota and Inuit.» What kind of word is Cherokee here? | A type of food | A colour | A kind of weather | *The name of a Native American people
exercise: «The Cherokee language has its own writing system.» What does Cherokee describe in this sentence? | A tall mountain | *The language spoken by the Cherokee people | A school subject for maths | A famous car
exercise: «In the 1830s the USA forced the Cherokee off their lands to the west, and thousands died on the march known as the Trail of Tears.» What was the Trail of Tears? | A treaty signed in a city | A holiday trip to the seaside | A school sports day | *A forced march west, when many people died
test: «The Cherokee writing system was created by Sequoyah.» Who created the Cherokee writing system? | *Sequoyah, a Cherokee man who made a writing system for his language | Navajo people | Sequoyah | The USA government
test: Mia reads, «The Cherokee Nation is a modern self-governing nation.» What does this sentence tell you? | The Cherokee live only in the 1830s | The Cherokee are a car company | *The Cherokee Nation governs itself today | Cherokee is a kind of language and nothing else
exam: «Many Cherokee people now live in Oklahoma and North Carolina, but their ancestors first lived in the south-east of what is now the USA.» Where did the Cherokee originally live? | *The south-east of what is now the USA | Oklahoma | The north of Canada | North Carolina
